{"total_count":3,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/1132","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/1132/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/1132/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/1132/events","html_url":"https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/pull/1132","id":4121268957,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAD89ks7Mszzc","number":1132,"title":"docs: add cross-references between grouping functions (#921)","user":{"login":"r266-tech","id":233881301,"node_id":"U_kgDODfC-1Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/233881301?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/r266-tech","html_url":"https://github.com/r266-tech","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r266-tech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r266-tech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r266-tech/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r266-tech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r266-tech/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r266-tech/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r266-tech/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r266-tech/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/r266-tech/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-23T14:19:09Z","updated_at":"2026-03-24T14:39:19Z","closed_at":"2026-03-24T14:39:19Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/pulls/1132","html_url":"https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/pull/1132","diff_url":"https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/pull/1132.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/pull/1132.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-24T14:39:19Z"},"body":"Closes #921\n\n## Summary\nAdds cross-references between `groupby_transform`, `bucket`, and `map_reduce` to help users discover the right grouping function for their use case.\n\n## Changes\n- **bucket**: Added `.. seealso::` referencing `map_reduce` (simpler API when storage is not a concern) and `groupby_transform` (when elements are already adjacent)\n- **groupby_transform**: Extended the final paragraph to note that `bucket` or `map_reduce` handle non-adjacent groups, and added `.. seealso::`\n- **map_reduce**: Added `.. seealso::` referencing `bucket` (lazy evaluation) and `groupby_transform` (when elements are already adjacent)\n\nAll changes are documentation-only; no code behavior is modified.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/1132/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/1132/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/440","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/440/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/440/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/440/events","html_url":"https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/pull/440","id":642429869,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0NDM3NDQ5Mzkw","number":440,"title":"Add groupfunc to groupby_transform","user":{"login":"bbayles","id":1922815,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjI4MTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1922815?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles","html_url":"https://github.com/bbayles","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2020-06-20T19:10:20Z","updated_at":"2020-07-02T01:22:41Z","closed_at":"2020-07-02T01:22:37Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/pulls/440","html_url":"https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/pull/440","diff_url":"https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/pull/440.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/pull/440.patch","merged_at":"2020-07-02T01:22:37Z"},"body":"This PR adds the *groupfunc* argument to `groupby_transform`.\r\n\r\nThe docs for `groupby` have this caveat:\r\n> The returned group is itself an iterator that shares the underlying iterable with groupby(). Because the source is shared, when the groupby() object is advanced, the previous group is no longer visible. So, if that data is needed later, it should be stored as a list.\r\n\r\nThis has come up here before, e.g. [issue 307](https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/307#issuecomment-526356782).\r\n\r\nThe `groupby` argument makes it easy to do that `list`-ifying, plus whatever else you might want to do.\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/440/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/440/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/196","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/196/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/196/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/196/events","html_url":"https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/pull/196","id":296066441,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0MTY4MzgxODg1","number":196,"title":"Add map_reduce function","user":{"login":"bbayles","id":1922815,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjI4MTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1922815?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles","html_url":"https://github.com/bbayles","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbayles/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":10,"created_at":"2018-02-10T02:44:14Z","updated_at":"2018-07-04T16:16:11Z","closed_at":"2018-02-20T12:04:56Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/pulls/196","html_url":"https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/pull/196","diff_url":"https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/pull/196.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/more-itertools/more-itertools/pull/196.patch","merged_at":"2018-02-20T12:04:56Z"},"body":"Re: issue #195 , this PR adds a variant of the \"dirt simple map/reduce\" [recipe](https://code.activestate.com/recipes/577676-dirt-simple-mapreduce/?in=user-178123). \r\n\r\nPer the discussion in the issue, I've modified things a bit:\r\n* With the default arguments, this now scratches the itch I noted in PR #188: \"easily make a `defaultdict(list)`\"\r\n* The original asks that you filter in the `mapper` function; here I encourage users to filter using standard itertools idioms (generator expressions or list comprehensions). This keeps the functions passed in simple, such that they just have to do one thing.\r\n\r\nI think these modifications make the docstring easy to comprehend, which I usually see as a strong virtue:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1922815/36057848-ecf028e2-0dd9-11e8-9b4b-eb1cd4598ec7.png)\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/196/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/more-itertools/more-itertools/issues/196/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}